BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:launch-526b4a0f-f0c9-4a20-9066-e9fc8c79307b@readout
DTSTAMP:20270330T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270330
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270331
SUMMARY:Launch: PLATO
DESCRIPTION:Ariane 62 · Arianespace Plato\, for PLAnetary Transits and Os
 cillations of stars\, is a European Space Agency (ESA) mission with 26 ca
 meras to study terrestrial exoplanets in orbits up to the habitable zone 
 of Sun-like stars. Its goal is to measure the sizes of exoplanets and dis
 cover exomoons and rings around them\, as well as characterise planets' h
 ost stars by studying tiny light variations in the starlight it receives.
  (no earlier than this date) Source: Launch Library 2 (The Space Devs).
LOCATION:Guiana Space Centre\, French Guiana
URL:https://ll.thespacedevs.com/2.3.0/launches/526b4a0f-f0c9-4a20-9066-e9f
 c8c79307b/
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:launch-0c69c87a-a253-4cdd-b83f-f434ff0f666b@readout
DTSTAMP:20270330T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270330
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270331
SUMMARY:Launch: Soyuz MS-30
DESCRIPTION:Soyuz 2.1a · Russian Federal Space Agency (ROSCOSMOS) Soyuz M
 S-30 will carry two cosmonauts and one astronaut to the International Spa
 ce Station aboard the Soyuz spacecraft from the Baikonur Cosmodrome in Ka
 zakhstan. The crew consists of Roscosmos cosmonauts Dmitri Petelin and Ko
 nstantin Borisov\, as well as NASA astronaut Deniz Burnham. (no earlier t
 han this date) Source: Launch Library 2 (The Space Devs).
LOCATION:Baikonur Cosmodrome\, Republic of Kazakhstan
URL:https://ll.thespacedevs.com/2.3.0/launches/0c69c87a-a253-4cdd-b83f-f43
 4ff0f666b/
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:launch-eda0f3bb-3a5e-438f-bdba-9dab2a86c281@readout
DTSTAMP:20270330T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270330
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270331
SUMMARY:Launch: TSIS-2
DESCRIPTION:Electron · Rocket Lab The Total and Spectral Solar Irradiance
  Sensor 2 (TSIS-2) is a satellite designed by NASA to measure the Sun's e
 nergy input to Earth. TSIS-2 comprises two instruments\, the Total Irradi
 ance Monitor (TIM)\, and the spectral Irradiance Monitor (SIM). TIM measu
 res total brightness and SIM measures spectral irradiance over a waveleng
 th range that includes 96% of the energy in the solar spectrum. Both in (
 no earlier than this date) Source: Launch Library 2 (The Space Devs).
LOCATION:Rocket Lab Launch Complex 1\, Mahia Peninsula\, New Zealand
URL:https://ll.thespacedevs.com/2.3.0/launches/eda0f3bb-3a5e-438f-bdba-9da
 b2a86c281/
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
